# Line-endings for shell scripts. cmd.exe mis-parses LF-only .bat/.cmd files
# (silent closes, skipped parenthesized blocks), so Windows scripts are kept
# byte-for-byte as CRLF in the repository (-text = no line-ending conversion
# on checkout OR archive download). Keep .bat/.cmd/.ps1 written with CRLF and
# .sh with LF in the working tree; Git will not normalise either.
*.bat -text
*.cmd -text
*.ps1 -text
*.sh  text eol=lf
